  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>It appears the Fedora Repository Webapp (3.1) is always expected at <a href=\"http://host:port/fedora/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://host:port/fedora/</a>. I wish to run the Webapp at <a href=\"http://host:port/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://host:port/</a>, as the \"root\" Web application on that host. We are dedicating a unique hostname to Fedora, it makes sense to have it respond to the shortest URL possible. </p>\n\n<p>To be totally honest I haven't even tried this &#8211; what I've seen doesn't make me believe it's feasible. I'd love to be proven wrong.</p>\n\n",
